angelina jolie opens up about how a  major blind spot in the medical field  has  impacted her children when you have that  many children  they really take care of each other in a  recent article for time  the 46 year old actress interviews  malone mcquenday  a 21 year old medical student who's on a  mission to teach  other aspiring doctors how conditions  and diseases can be present in non-white  patients  in the piece angelina writes that malone  started his project after learning that  quote  almost all the images and data used in  its teachings were based on studies of  white  patients which can lead to quote  misdiagnosis  suffering and even death and the  oscar-winning actress says she's seen  the problem  first hand with her own kids of course  angie and her ex brad pitt  share 19 year old maddox 17 year old pax  16 year old zahara 15 year old shiloh  and 12 year old twins  knox and vivian angelina explains quote  i have children from different  backgrounds  and i know when there was a rash that  everybody got  it looked drastically different  depending on their skin color  but whenever i looked at medical charts  the reference point was always white  skin  the maleficent star also says she  experienced something similar  after her eldest daughter zahara who is  black  had a procedure done last year quote  recently my daughter zahara whom i  adopted from ethiopia  had surgery and afterward a nurse told  me to call them if her skin  turned pink malone says that experiences  like angie's are the kind of thing he  noticed  very early on quote there's a language  and a culture that exists in the medical  profession  because it's been done for so many years  and because we are still doing it so  many years later  it doesn't seem like it's a problem but  malone says angie's experience perfectly  illustrates why it is a problem  quote that's a very problematic  statement for some groups of the  population  because it's just not going to happen in  that way  and if you're unaware you probably won't  call the doctor  back in march 2020 angie opened up about  zahara's surgery in an essay written for  time magazine  revealing that one of her younger  daughters also had hip surgery around  the same time  quote i have watched my daughter's care  for one another  my youngest daughter studied the nurses  with her sister and then assisted the  next time  i saw how all my girls so easily stopped  everything and put each other first  and felt the joy of being of service to  those they love they wrangle me  honestly they're more together zahara is  the most organized in the family  angelina has also been vocal about her  own medical scares  which included undergoing a preventative  double mastectomy in 2013  and having her ovaries and fallopian  tubes removed in 2015  as a preventative measure against cancer  try to rediscover that  that strength within in 2019 she told  harper's bazaar quote  my body has been through a lot over the  past decade  particularly the past four years and i  have both the visible  and invisible scars to show for it  adding quote  life takes many turns sometimes you get  hurt  you see those you love in pain and you  can't be as free and open as your spirit  desires  it's not new or old but i do feel the  blood returning to my body  you
 

